---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="Clinical Standards, Ethics & Confidentiality" 
  description="How Nepal Hypnosis protects your privacy, safety and rights: confidentiality and its limits, consent, supervision, records, fees, complaints and referral."
>
  <section class="bg-gradient-to-b from-[#F5F1EA] to-white pt-16 pb-12 border-b border-[#e2e8f0]">
    <div class="container-nh max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4">
      <h1 class="mt-4 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold text-[#173A7A] leading-tight">Clinical Standards & Ethics</h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-[#475569] leading-relaxed">
        Trust is the foundation of therapy. This page explains plainly how we protect you, what you can expect from us, and what we expect of ourselves. Nepal Hypnosis has been operating in Kathmandu since 2012.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-12 bg-white">
    <div class="container-nh max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 space-y-10 text-[#475569] leading-relaxed">
      
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#173A7A] mb-4">Our commitments to you</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-3">
          <li><strong>Strict confidentiality:</strong> What you tell us stays within the clinic. Records are held securely and shared only with your written consent, or in the limited situations below.</li>
          <li><strong>Limits of confidentiality:</strong> We explain these at your first session. In rare cases we may need to share information: when there is a serious risk to your life or someone else's, when a child or vulnerable person is at risk, or when the law requires it.</li>
          <li><strong>Informed consent:</strong> Before therapy starts, we explain the approach, how long it may take, benefits, risks, and fees. You can stop at any time.</li>
          <li><strong>Individualised care:</strong> Treatment plans respect your background, culture, values and autonomy.</li>
          <li><strong>Honest practice:</strong> We do not guarantee results or cures, and we do not claim more than the evidence supports.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#173A7A] mb-4">Safety and emergencies</h2>
        <p>Nepal Hypnosis is not an emergency or crisis service. If you are in immediate danger, call <strong>1166</strong> or go to the nearest emergency department. During therapy, if we are concerned about your safety, we will discuss a safety plan with you.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#173A7A] mb-4">Your rights</h2>
        <p>You have the right to ask questions about your treatment, see or ask about your records, be treated respectfully, get a second opinion, and stop therapy at any time.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>